WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.840
Euclid has released images of 900 million galaxies spanning an area equal to 9,500 full moons. This is Fascinating Frontiers, Episode 252. Amino acids in Bennu grains, Katie Spicer fitting out a lunar lander, and an Ohio astronaut who trained under the sea. The European Space Agency's wide and deep surveys hold roughly 2.5 trillion pixels in 1.7 million gigabytes. Spectra from 160 million sources sit in the release

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.660
piece, along with 60 million quasar candidates.

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:38.040
Some galaxies date from an epoch when the universe was only 700 million years old.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:44.020
The observations map cosmic structures and gravitational lensing distortions, as Euclid

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:49.480
covers one-third of the sky across a six-year mission, producing around 20 new images each

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:49.780
day.

00:00:50.805 --> 00:00:57.025
Benu grains contain the amino acid beta-alanine, universe today notes, the same molecule as in

00:00:57.025 --> 00:01:00.825
purchase and meteorite, which landed in Australia in 1969.

00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:06.045
Those grains still hold chemical fingerprints laid down billions of years ago in the gas

00:01:06.045 --> 00:01:07.925
and dust disk around the young sun.

00:01:08.965 --> 00:01:14.105
Isotopic ratios read Adam by Adam inside single molecules, separate formation pathways,

00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:19.065
that ran at different distances from the sun, and under different temperatures and radiation.

00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:24.845
Some of those beta-alanine molecules carry isotopic signatures that fit cold chemistry in

00:01:24.845 --> 00:01:28.425
the outer disk, while others fit warmer conditions closer in.

00:01:29.125 --> 00:01:33.585
The contrast survived in the return samples because the parent bodies never got hot enough

00:01:33.585 --> 00:01:38.445
to wipe it out, and the measurements work as time capsules of chemical diversity across

00:01:38.445 --> 00:01:42.225
the solar nebula, while planets and asteroids were coming together.

00:01:42.805 --> 00:01:48.385
Exactly how far apart the two formation zones sat is still unknown, and it is not yet clear

00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:52.605
whether other amino acids or grains from other asteroids show the same spread.

00:01:52.605 --> 00:01:58.385
Lab work that pairs those isotopic readings with dynamical models of the disc will test

00:01:58.385 --> 00:02:03.105
whether the pattern needs radial mixing or whether static formation zones can explain

00:02:03.105 --> 00:02:03.885
it on their own.

00:02:04.952 --> 00:02:10.332
Katie Spicer now leads integration for Blue Origins Blue Moon Mark II Lander, one of two

00:02:10.332 --> 00:02:15.372
commercial systems, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration, or NASA, selected

00:02:15.372 --> 00:02:16.952
for Artemis crewed landings.

00:02:17.352 --> 00:02:21.332
