00:04:40.531 --> 00:04:47.331
A Hubble gallery, NASA reports, shows a range of strong lensing layouts created by foreground galaxies.

00:04:47.931 --> 00:04:52.551
Models drawn from the images will help measure mass distributions including dark matter.

00:04:53.091 --> 00:04:58.851
Tiny flaws in the arcs could expose dark matter clumps between 1 million and 1 billion solar masses.

